 rom UK) starts Mon 02 Aug 2027 in Totality path: Cádiz/Tarifa\, Gibraltar
 \, northern Morocco\, Tunisia\, Libya\, Luxor (Egypt). Now's the time to s
 ort flights\, tickets and somewhere to sleep.\n\nThe eclipse of the decade
 . Totality reaches about 6 m 23 s near Luxor\, one of the longest totaliti
 es over land this century. The path of darkness crosses southern Spain and
  the Strait of Gibraltar\, so Tarifa or Cádiz is a cheap flight away. You
  get midday darkness\, stars\, the corona and a 360° sunset. From the UK 
 it's only a ~35% partial (around 09:00–11:00 BST). Go to the path. Do no
 t miss this.\n\nStatus of the event date: ✅ Confirmed\nOfficial info: ht
 tps://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar/2027-august-2
